# Scope Before Code

When the request leaves a material product, interface, architecture, rollout, or migration choice unresolved, state the intended outcome and the key decision before choosing an implementation. Record assumptions that could change the result.

For clear local work, inspect the repository, choose the established pattern, and proceed. Do not create an approval or planning loop unless the user requested one or the unresolved decision needs their input.
